  <p>This substructure might be proper if <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> $\cap$ <span data-field="D_val">{{ D_val }}</span> is finite for all <span data-field="i">{{ i }}</span> $\in$ <span data-field="w">{{ w }}</span>. If <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> is not proper, then <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> is a boolean algebra and hence D must be h-simple inside <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span>. By Lemma <span data-field="lemma_ref_12">{{ lemma_ref_12 }}</span>, <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is a c.e. set.</p>
  <p>If <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is D-maximal, then the converse holds. Assume that <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is D-maximal and <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> is a boolean algebra. Then there exists a set <span data-field="W_val">{{ W_val }}</span> such that either <span data-field="W_val">{{ W_val }}</span> $\subseteq$ <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> or <span data-field="W_val">{{ W_val }}</span> $\cup$ <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> = <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span>.</p>
  <p>We conclude that <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is c.e. if <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> is a boolean algebra.</p>
  <p>In <span data-field="§5</span>, we show that D-maximal sets of Types <span data-field="type_ref_5">{{ §5</span>, we show that D-maximal sets of Types <span data-field= }}</span> are h-simple-like. We construct these three Types of sets, we will ensure that D is h-simple inside <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span>, for all <span data-field="i">{{ i }}</span>, and moreover, for all <span data-field="i">{{ i }}</span>, <span data-field="D_i">{{ D_i }}</span> $\cap$ <span data-field="R_i">{{ R_i }}</span> is infinite and noncomputable. Our construction will show that <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is h-simple-like.</p>
  <p>Corollary <span data-field="corollary_ref_5">{{ corollary_ref_5 }}</span>. There is half of a splitting of a h-simple set that is D-maximal and Type <span data-field="type_val_54">{{ type_val_54 }}</span>.</p>
  <p>Again, we can ask what kind of split is needed. By Lemma <span data-field="lemma_ref_13">{{ lemma_ref_13 }}</span> and <span data-field="lemma_ref_6">{{ lemma_ref_6 }}</span>, it can be a trivial or Friedberg splitting. Note that Corollary <span data-field="corollary_ref_5">{{ corollary_ref_5 }}</span> as presented is a trivial splitting. We can also construct a Friedberg splitting of a h-simple set that is D-maximal and Type <span data-field="type_val_55">{{ type_val_55 }}</span>. They also directly prove that these splits cannot be trivial or Friedberg.</p>
