  <h3 class="section-heading">3.5. Questions.</h3>
  <p>First, is it natural to ask as we did in Question <span data-field="question_ref_3">{{ question_ref_3 }}</span> if all the Types are definable. In a related vein, it is natural to wonder whether Types <span data-field="type_val_56">{{ type_val_56 }}</span> are definable. We show that they are not definable. We construct the D-maximal sets of Types <span data-field="type_val_57">{{ type_val_57 }}</span> and verify uniformity for all <span data-field="i">{{ i }}</span> $\ge$ <span data-field="0">{{ 0 }}</span>, <span data-field="D_i">{{ D_i }}</span> $\cap$ <span data-field="R_i">{{ R_i }}</span> is infinite and noncomputable. Perhaps one could further divide Types <span data-field="type_val_58">{{ type_val_58 }}</span> into smaller types, but we do not explore this possibility here. We suggest that the reader look at <span data-field="ref_3">{{ ref_3 }}</span> before considering these questions.</p>
  <p>We also asked in Question <span data-field="question_ref_4">{{ question_ref_4 }}</span> whether Type <span data-field="type_val_59">{{ type_val_59 }}</span> sets must be splits of r-maximal sets.</p>
  <h3 class="section-heading">4. D-MAXIMAL SETS OF ALL TYPES EXIST</h3>
  <p>The next theorem is the main result of the paper.</p>
  <p>Theorem <span data-field="theorem_ref_3">{{ theorem_ref_3 }}</span>. There are complete and incomplete D-maximal sets of each Type. Moreover, for any D-maximal set <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span>:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is maximal iff <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is Type <span data-field="type_val_60">{{ type_val_60 }}</span>.</li>
    <li><span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is maximal iff <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is Type <span data-field="type_val_61">{{ type_val_61 }}</span>.</li>
    <li><span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is maximal iff <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is Type <span data-field="type_val_62">{{ type_val_62 }}</span>.</li>
    <li><span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is h-maximal iff <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is Type <span data-field="type_val_63">{{ type_val_63 }}</span>.</li>
    <li><span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is h-maximal iff <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is Type <span data-field="type_val_64">{{ type_val_64 }}</span>.</li>
    <li><span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is an A-special list iff <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is Type <span data-field="type_val_65">{{ type_val_65 }}</span>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>So, for each of the first six Types, the D-maximal sets of that Type form a single orbit. The D-maximal sets of each of the remaining four Types break up into infinitely many orbits.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
