  <p>In <span data-field="§4.2</span> we present a construction of D-maximal sets of Type <span data-field="type_val_66">{{ §4.2</span> we present a construction of D-maximal sets of Type <span data-field= }}</span> (by taking an appropriate splitting of an atomless r-maximal set). We also show that these sets break up into infinitely many orbits, and we show that they are not definable. We also show that they are not h-simple-like. We also show that they are not h-maximal. We also show that they are not A-special list.</p>
  <p>Lemma <span data-field="lemma_ref_14">{{ lemma_ref_14 }}</span>. A set <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is simple iff D(<span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span>) = <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span>. So, a simple set is D-maximal for all <span data-field="i">{{ i }}</span> whether <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> $\subseteq$ <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span> or <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> $\subsetneq$ <span data-field="R_val">{{ R_val }}</span>. Hence, the first three subclasses of Theorem <span data-field="theorem_ref_3">{{ theorem_ref_3 }}</span> hold.</p>
  <p>Lemma <span data-field="lemma_ref_15">{{ lemma_ref_15 }}</span>. A set <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is D-maximal and Type <span data-field="type_val_67">{{ type_val_67 }}</span> iff <span data-field="A_val">{{ A_val }}</span> is h-maximal.</p>
