    splits of a hsimple set $H$ of a given kind of flavor $B$. Let $B$ be a $\Sigma_2$ boolean algebra
    with infinitely many pairwise incomparable elements. We call a subset $\{b_i\}_{i \in \omega}$ of $B$
    a skeleton for $B$ if the elements in $\{b_i\}_{i \in \omega}$ are pairwise incomparable and, for every
    element $b \in B$, either $b$ or its complement is below the join of finitely many elements
    in $\{b_i\}_{i \in \omega}$. If $\{b_i\}_{i \in \omega}$ is a skeleton for $B$ and $B \cong \text{Fin}(\{b_i\}_{i \in \omega})$, then
    $B \cong \text{Fin}(\{b_i\}_{i \in \omega})$.
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: justify; margin-top: 20px;">
